# 🔗 CodeAlpha URL Shortener

A backend REST API built with **Node.js**, **Express**, and **MongoDB** that shortens long URLs and provides JWT-based user authentication with secure HTTP-only cookies.

---

## 🚀 Features

- **URL Shortening** — Convert long URLs into short, shareable links
- **URL Redirection** — Short URLs redirect to the original long URL
- **Visit Tracking** — Tracks visit history with timestamps
- **User Authentication** — Register, Login, and Logout with JWT
- **Secure Cookies** — Tokens stored in HTTP-only cookies (XSS-safe)
- **Password Hashing** — Passwords hashed with bcrypt

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| Node.js | Runtime |
| Express.js | Web Framework |
| MongoDB | Database |
| Mongoose | ODM |
| JSON Web Token | Authentication |
| bcrypt | Password Hashing |
| nanoid | Short ID Generation |
| dotenv | Environment Variables |

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
Url_shortener/
├── controllers/
│   ├── authcontroller.js      # Register, Login, Logout logic
│   └── urlcontroller.js       # URL shortening & redirect logic
├── models/
│   ├── user.js                # User schema (name, email, password)
│   └── url.js                 # URL schema (shortUrl, longUrl, visitHistory)
├── routes/
│   ├── authroutes.js          # Auth endpoints
│   └── urlroutes.js           # URL endpoints
├── utilities/
│   ├── generateToken.js       # JWT token generation
│   └── verifyToken.js         # JWT token verification
├── .env                       # Environment variables (not committed)
├── .gitignore
├── connection.js              # MongoDB connection
├── index.js                   # Entry point
├── package.json
└── README.md
```

---

## ⚙️ Setup & Installation

### Prerequisites
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v18+)
- [MongoDB](https://www.mongodb.com/) (local or Atlas)

### Steps

1. **Clone the repository**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/Krishna-Kumar0/CodeAlpha_URL-SHORTENER.git
   cd CodeAlpha_URL-SHORTENER
   ```

2. **Install dependencies**
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```

3. **Create a `.env` file** in the root directory
   ```env
   MONGO_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017/url_shortener
   JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key_here
   BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
   ```

4. **Start the server**
   ```bash
   npm start
   ```

   The server will run on `http://localhost:5000`

---

## 📡 API Endpoints

### 🔐 Authentication

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Body |
|--------|----------|-------------|------|
| POST | `/auth/register` | Register a new user | `{ name, email, password }` |
| POST | `/auth/login` | Login | `{ email, password }` |
| POST | `/auth/logout` | Logout (clears cookie) | — |

### 🔗 URL Shortener

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Body |
|--------|----------|-------------|------|
| POST | `/url/shorten` | Shorten a URL | `{ url: "https://example.com" }` |
| GET | `/url/:shortid` | Redirect to original URL | — |

---

## 📝 Example Usage (Postman)

### Shorten a URL
```
POST http://localhost:5000/url/shorten
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://www.google.com"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "shortUrl": "http://localhost:5000/url/aB3xK9z"
}
```

### Visit the shortened URL
```
GET http://localhost:5000/url/aB3xK9z
→ Redirects to https://www.google.com
```

